# Quarto build output
/_site/
/.quarto/

# Private drafts: old Jekyll-site writing kept for personal reference only.
# drafts/ is NOT excluded from _quarto.yml's render list (Quarto's auto
# "listing:" needs the folder to be part of the project to build the
# drafts/index.qmd timeline), so a full `quarto render` DOES emit
# _site/drafts/*.html. This line is the real privacy boundary: it keeps the
# drafts/ source off the public repo -- and it's why drafts/ never shows up
# in GitHub Desktop's changes list at all.
#
# .github/workflows/publish.yml (the GitHub Actions deploy pipeline) already
# runs `rm -rf _site/drafts` after rendering, before the build reaches
# Pages, so the *published* site stays clean automatically. That step only
# matters for automated/CI publishing though -- if you ever render and copy
# _site/ up manually instead, remember to strip _site/drafts yourself first.
/drafts/

**/*.quarto_ipynb
